@startuml
autonumber
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #2F5D7C
  LifeLineBorderColor #2F5D7C
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FBFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #2F5D7C
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF4FF
}

actor "Framework E2E\nprovisioner" as Test
participant "Containerlab E2E\nlifecycle" as Lab
participant "Framework network /\nendpoint managers" as Framework
participant "OVSDB management API" as Mgmt
database "OVN NBDB" as NB
participant "ovn-northd" as Northd
database "OVN SBDB" as SB
participant "Framework endpoint\nexporter" as Exporter
participant "managed gobgpd\n(k8gobgp DaemonSet)" as GoBGP
participant "External FRR peer\n+ remote workload" as FRR
participant "OVSDB Type-2\nroute importer" as Importer
participant "OVN/OVSDB\nprogrammer" as Programmer
participant "ovn-controller" as Controller
participant "OVN/OVS dataplane" as OVS

note over Test,Importer
  Dedicated one-chassis test. No evpn-cni, Multus, NAD,
  CNI ADD/CHECK/DEL, or Netlink remote writer.
  The OVSDB importer is explicitly selected for this network.
end note

== Disposable laboratory ==
Test -> Lab : reserve exact topology; deploy native kind + FRR
Lab -> Lab : verify ownership, readiness and management CA
Lab --> Test : private kubeconfig and environment receipts
Test -> Test : deploy OVN/OVS and managed k8gobgp
note over Test,GoBGP
  BGPConfiguration CRD -> k8gobgp reconciliation -> managed gobgpd.
  Manager + daemon share one upstream DaemonSet image.
  Framework clients use local Unix gRPC; no competing upstream Netlink writer.
end note

== Framework provisioning ==
Test -> Mgmt : AddNetwork(logical switch)
Mgmt -> NB : create Framework logical switch
NB --> Mgmt : network status
Test -> Framework : Ensure endpoint A/B
Framework -> NB : create owned endpoint Logical_Switch_Ports
Framework -> OVS : ensure identity-owned local attachment
NB -> Northd : logical network / port configuration
Northd -> SB : logical flows and Port_Binding
SB --> Controller : local chassis Port_Binding
Controller -> OVS : claim local binding; program forwarding
Exporter -> NB : observe Framework-owned endpoint identity
Exporter -> SB : verify local chassis binding
Exporter -> GoBGP : AddPath Type-2 MAC and MAC/IP; retain UUID
GoBGP -> FRR : local endpoint EVPN routes

== Remote route import and OVSDB programming ==
FRR -> GoBGP : remote Type-2 MAC/IP route
Importer -> GoBGP : poll complete EVPN RIB snapshot
GoBGP --> Importer : RD, RT, VNI, MAC/IP, next hop
Importer -> Importer : validate route and import policy
Importer -> Programmer : reconcile route-derived tunnel
Programmer -> OVS : ensure owned provider bridge and bridge mapping
Programmer -> NB : ensure owned localnet LSP on configured physnet
Programmer -> OVS : ensure owned VXLAN interface and port
NB -> Northd : localnet configuration
Northd -> SB : localnet logical state / binding
SB --> Controller : reconcile localnet forwarding
Controller -> OVS : program OVN/OVS forwarding state

== Bidirectional workload traffic ==
Test -> OVS : ping local endpoint to remote workload
OVS -> FRR : VXLAN traffic through OVS tunnel
FRR --> OVS : reverse VXLAN traffic
OVS --> Test : bidirectional result
Test -> Test : correlate endpoint, underlay, FRR,\nVXLAN and remote-workload captures

== Local endpoint withdrawal and survivor ==
Test -> Framework : delete local endpoint A
Framework -> NB : remove endpoint A LSP
Exporter -> GoBGP : asynchronously DeletePath exact UUIDs for A
GoBGP -> FRR : withdraw endpoint A
Test -> FRR : verify A absent and B remains
Test -> OVS : verify endpoint B still reaches remote workload

== Remote route withdrawal and owned cleanup ==
Test -> FRR : remove remote workload bridge attachment
FRR -> GoBGP : withdraw remote Type-2 route\n(peer remains established)
Importer -> GoBGP : observe authoritative RIB without remote route
GoBGP --> Importer : route absent
Importer -> Programmer : reconcile empty remote snapshot
Programmer -> OVS : delete owned VXLAN interface / port
Programmer -> NB : remove owned localnet LSP
Programmer -> OVS : remove owned bridge mapping
NB -> Northd : localnet removed
Northd -> SB : localnet path withdrawn asynchronously
Controller -> OVS : remove controller-owned localnet patch ports
Programmer -> OVS : retry owned provider-bridge deletion when safe
Test -> GoBGP : verify remote Type-2 absent and Type-3 remains
Test -> FRR : verify remote Type-2 absent; peer remains established
Test -> OVS : verify pre-existing unowned VXLAN interfaces remain
Test -> NB : verify endpoint B remains; remote localnet LSP absent
Test -> Framework : delete endpoint B and DelNetwork
Framework -> NB : remove endpoint and Framework logical switch
Test -> Test : verify no stale owned OVN/OVS state and restore inventories
Test -> Lab : collect diagnostics; destroy exact owned topology
Lab --> Test : owned resources absent; unrelated resources preserved

note over Importer,Programmer
  The mapping is route network/VNI/next hop to the owned provider
  path; MAC and optional IP are validated and retained in route
  ownership metadata. The current opt-in integration supports one network
  and one remote VTEP.
end note
note over Programmer,OVS
  Cross-database steps are not atomic. Retry/refuse on partial cleanup;
  never force-delete controller-owned patches or foreign ports.
  Partial per-MAC learned-FDB invalidation is not accepted.
end note
@enduml
